    "https://nebraskamed.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Omaha-NE/Welcome-Center-Coordinator_REQ-38425": {
      "title": "Welcome Center Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n\"Prepare to be the best\" is not just a saying at Clarkson College; it's part of our Mission. Every member of our team plays a vital role in preparing students to professionally provide high quality, ethical and compassionate health care services and become the best in their chosen field. Clarkson College is currently seeking a College Welcome Center Coordinator. The College Welcome Center Coordinator will be the face of Clarkson College, providing a welcoming, inclusive, and professional experience for all stakeholders. This position will coordinate communication between internal and external entities/guests and ensure that the experience meets or exceeds expectations.  Additionally, this position will provide support to college constituents to ensure activities and operations of the College Welcome Center are effectively organized, coordinated, and implemented. The Coordinator will interact with 1250 plus students and employees within the College along with many guests from outside the College.  Required Qualifications: •    High school education or equivalent required. •    Minimum of two years in an office or administrative role required.     •    Excellent written and verbal communication skills required.   •    Excellent interpersonal, critical thinking, and organizational skills required.    •    Experience operating a personal computer and proficiency in MS Office required.  Preferred Qualifications •   Associates or bachelor’s degree in communication or business, or related field preferred. •    Ability to understand federal regulations and policies related to accreditation and student records preferred.   Why Clarkson College: Clarkson College is a private college in Omaha, Nebraska and is known for leading the education and training needs in our region for over 137 years. Clarkson College’s core values consist of learning, excellence, integrity, commitment, and caring.   Recognized as a 2025 Great College to Work For, Clarkson College offers a flexible work schedule and family-friendly benefits to all our employees. Paid Time Off Retirement match contribution Medical, dental and vision insurance Tuition benefits for employees, dependents, and spouses. Support for Community Involvement Wellness Incentives Working at Clarkson College means making a commitment to teaching and developing future health care leaders. Your work will be key to the success of your co-workers as you help our students feel comfortable, prepared and confident to enter this rewarding field."
    },
    "https://nebraskamed.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Omaha-NE/English-Language-Learner-Tutor_REQ-38324": {
      "title": "English Language Learner Tutor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nPart time\n\n\"Prepare to be the best\" is not just a saying at Clarkson College; it's part of our Mission. Every member of our team plays a vital role in preparing students to professionally provide high quality, ethical and compassionate health care services and become the best in their chosen field. Clarkson College is seeking to hire a tutor to assist English Language Learner (ELL) students. This position will provide academic tutoring and support to college students who are English Language Learners (ELLs), assist students in developing academic language proficiency, understanding course content, improving study skills, and navigating academic culture. Tutors will work with students individually and potentially in small groups across various subjects, with a focus on language development. The tutor will assess, assist and encourage the students in the learning processes. Tutors review materials used in classes, explain various topics, and answer questions.  The tutor will meet one on one with students or in a small group in a virtual setting by appointment. The ideal candidate will be able to provide 5-10 hours of availability each week excluding Clarkson College breaks. Required Qualifications: •    Bachelor’s degree in English, TESOL, Applied Linguistics, Education, or a related field is required •   Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to explain concepts clearly and patiently required. •    An awareness of the challenges faced by English Language Learners in an academic setting required.  •    Understanding of diverse cultural and linguistic backgrounds required. •    Ability to work effectively with students from various proficiency levels and academic disciplines required. •    Reliability, punctuality, and strong organizational skills required. •    Ability to maintain confidentiality and adhere to college policies required.  Preferred Qualifications: •    ESL certification (e.g., TESOL, TEFL) preferred. •    Previous tutoring experience preferred. •    Basic understanding of medical terminology preferred.  Working at Clarkson College means making a commitment to teaching and developing future health care leaders. Your work will be key to the success of your co-workers as you help our students feel comfortable, prepared and confident to enter this rewarding field."
    },
    "https://nebraskamed.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Omaha-NE/Nurse-Aide-Instructor_REQ-38073": {
      "title": "Nurse Aide Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\n\"Prepare to be the best\" is not just a saying at Clarkson College; it's part of our Mission. Every member of our team plays a vital role in preparing students to professionally provide high quality, ethical and compassionate health care services and become the best in their chosen field. Clarkson College is currently seeking a Nurse Aide Instructor to teach Nurse Aide Course and/or the Medication Aide Course and other Professional Development health care courses utilizing a college or State of Nebraska approved curriculum. This position is currently only open to current Clarkson College employees. Required Qualifications: Minimum of two (2) years nursing experience required. Minimum of six (6) months experience teaching nurse aide, medication aide or other related health care courses OR minimum of six (6) months experience supervising nurse aides or nurses required. Associate degree in nursing required. Excellent communication and instructional skills required. Theoretical and clinical competency required. Ability to work with a varied population of individuals required. Ability to multi-task while in classroom and at clinical site required. Proficient in use of MS Word, PowerPoint and Excel required. Proficient in use of classroom equipment (computer, projector, electronic bulletin board, TV, and DVD player) required. Proficient in use of office equipment (files, duplicating machine, fax machine, telephone) required. Proficient in use of medical facility equipment (mechanical bed, wheelchair, patient lifts, etc.) required. Current State of Nebraska RN license or compact agreement state RN license required. Current American Heart Association certification in Basic Life Support for Health Care Providers required. Current valid motor vehicle operator's license required. Ability to meet and maintain insurability requirements as defined by the fleet automobile liability insurance carrier required. Preferred Qualifications: One year or more experience working in a long-term care facility or with a geriatric population preferred. Bachelor's degree in nursing preferred Clarkson College is an Equal Opportunity Employer: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, marital status, sex, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity and protected veterans’ status. Working at Clarkson College means making a commitment to teaching and developing future health care leaders. Your work will be key to the success of your co-workers as you help our students feel comfortable, prepared and confident to enter this rewarding field."
